1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,219
You creep through a dark cave and step into

2
00:00:03,219 --> 00:00:05,164
a pit. In the classic game,

3
00:00:05,164 --> 00:00:07,434
that one wrong step ends the hunt,

4
00:00:07,434 --> 00:00:09,704
and you can't do anything about it.

5
00:00:10,700 --> 00:00:14,279
Hunt the Wumpus remakes the 1973 cave game in

6
00:00:14,279 --> 00:00:17,460
Unity. Now a hazard starts a trivia duel,

7
00:00:17,460 --> 00:00:21,436
with a question a language model writes on the spot.

8
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:24,770
The hex map of the 30-room cave.

9
00:00:24,770 --> 00:00:26,801
Colour tells you about your room,

10
00:00:26,801 --> 00:00:28,832
and text warns of neighbouring rooms,

11
00:00:28,832 --> 00:00:30,524
like a smell of wumpus.

12
00:00:31,300 --> 00:00:33,314
A hazard opens a trivia duel.

13
00:00:33,314 --> 00:00:36,335
A right answer gets you out of the pit

14
00:00:36,335 --> 00:00:38,013
or drives the monster off.

15
00:00:38,800 --> 00:00:41,703
The cave stays loaded in one scene.

16
00:00:41,703 --> 00:00:45,020
A hazard loads the trivia scene on top,

17
00:00:45,020 --> 00:00:48,753
which asks OpenAI, or falls back to offline questions.

18
00:00:49,800 --> 00:00:54,476
Try it at github dot com slash Mallard64 slash Wumpus.
